      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Clonidine substantially reduces the pain and cramping of dysmenorrhea. The mechanisms for this effect may lie in increased release of analgesic opioids. It is suggested that perhaps a thromboxane synthetase inhibitor such as ginger which activates endorphin receptors may also be an effective treatment."},
